/-- Let ~ be the equivalence relation on {0,...,n-1} generated by allowedSwaps. Whenever the function returns a result r, there exists a permutation π of the set {0,...,n-1} (a bijection from {0,...,n-1} to itself) such that for every i with 0 <= i < n we have i ~ π(i), and the number of indices i with 0 <= i < n and source[π(i)] != target[i] is exactly r.
